        Return a boolean indicating whether the data is contiguous.

        Parameters
        ----------
        None

        Examples
        --------
        >>> import numpy as np
        >>> x = np.ma.array([1, 2, 3])
        >>> x.iscontiguous()
        True

        `iscontiguous` returns one of the flags of the masked array:

        >>> x.flags
          C_CONTIGUOUS : True
          F_CONTIGUOUS : True
          OWNDATA : False
          WRITEABLE : True
          ALIGNED : True
          WRITEBACKIFCOPY : False

